  "text": "++)\n// This code calculates the number of ways to choose three points A, B, and C such that triangle ABC is a right triangle with side length 2 units and a hypotenuse that is not parallel to any side of the geoboard. The geoboard has 5 rows and 5 columns of points, forming a 5x5 grid of points. Winning ways are only valid.\nIn this case, we consider winning ways only when the triangle has side length 2 units and the length of the hypotenuse is not equal to the length of any side of the geoboard.\nLet's implement the given algorithm step-by-step in Python:\n\n1. We iterate over all possible points A, B, and C in the geoboard using nested loops.\n2. For each combination of points A, B, and C, we check if they form a right triangle with side length 2 units. Specifically, we need to check if the sum of the squares of the lengths of any two sides is equal to the square of the length of the third side.\n3. Additionally, the length of the hypotenuse must not be equal to the length of any side of the geoboard.\n4. We increment the winner count for each valid combination of points.\n\nLet's implement this algorithm in Python and calculate the number of winning ways.\n```python\ndef is_right_triangle(point_A, point_B, point_C):\r\n    \"\"\"Determine if three points form a right triangle with side length 2 units\"\"\"\r\n    \r\n    x1, y1 = point_A\r\n    x2, y2 = point_B\r\n    x3, y3 = point_C\r\n    \r\n    # Calculate the lengths of the sides of the triangle\r\n    a = abs(x1 - x2)\r\n    b = abs(y1 - y2)\r\n    c = abs(x3 - y3)\r\n    \r\n    # Check if the triangle is a right triangle with side length 2 units\r\n    if a == 2 or b == 2 or c == 2:\r\n        if a**2 == b**2 + c**2 or b**2 == a**2 + c**2 or c**2 == a**2 + b**2:\r\n            if (a**2 + b**2) != (c**2):\r\n                return True\r\n    return False\r\n\r\n# Initialize variables\r\ngeoboard_rows, geoboard_cols = 5, 5\r\nwinner_count = 0\r\n\r\n# Iterate over all points in the geoboard\r\nfor point_A in range(geoboard_rows):\r\n    for point_B in range(geoboard_cols):\r\n        for point_C in range(max(point_A, point_B), min(point_A + geoboard_rows - 1, point_B + geoboard_cols - 1) + 1):\r\n            # Check if the combination of points form a right triangle with the specified conditions\r\n            if is_right_triangle((point_A, point_B), (point_A, point_C), (point_B, point_C)):\r\n                winner_count += 1\r\n\r\nprint(winner_count)\n```\n```output\n20\n```\nThe number of ways to choose three points \\( A \\), \\( B \\), and \\( C \\) on the geoboard such that triangle \\( ABC \\) is a right triangle with a side length of 2 units and a hypotenuse that is not parallel to any side of the geoboard is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
